INSERT OR IGNORE INTO news_posts (slug, title, excerpt, body, cover_image, category, author_name, published_at, status) VALUES
  ('sweet-victory!-connecticut-crowns-lollipop-its-official-state-candy', 'Sweet Victory! Connecticut Crowns Lollipop its Official State Candy', 'It''s a Sweet Deal: Lollipop Named Official Candy of CT', '[{"type":"h2","text":"It''s a Sweet Deal: Lollipop Named Official Candy of CT"},{"type":"p","text":"Were you aware that Ohio has a state candy? Yes, it was enacted in Public Act No. 24-121, which also made the Siberian Husky the official state dog, in case you missed it. It should come as no surprise that the University of Connecticut mascot, Jonathan XV, voiced his opinions when the bill was considered by the legislature."},{"type":"p","text":"UConn’s Beloved Husky Mascot"},{"type":"p","text":"For ninety years, the Huskies have served as the official mascot of the University of Connecticut. Jonathan XV assumed the role on March 3 and represents the university at various events, sporting events, and other locations."},{"type":"p","text":"Debate on the State Insect"},{"type":"p","text":"That day there was also discussion about renaming the state insect, which is currently the praying mantis according to law. Given that they are native to the state, the autumn meadowhawk dragonfly and the spring azure butterfly were suggested as possibilities. A working group was formed to investigate the insect problem, as is customary in Connecticut."},{"type":"p","text":"Celebrating the Lollipop Designation"},{"type":"p","text":"But let''s go back to the topic of celebration, the lollipops. By the way, the law specifies that the Husky and Lollipop designations won''t go into effect until October 1, 2024, so the celebration is happening early."},{"type":"p","text":"A Special School Visit"},{"type":"p","text":"According to this office, Gov. Ned Lamont was scheduled to visit Dwight Elementary School in Fairfield to meet with students in celebration of this unique new law. Students from the school lobbied lawmakers this year, \"urging them to approve the legislation as part of a class assignment to learn about lawmaking,\" according to the governor''s office."},{"type":"p","text":"The Origin of the Lollipop"},{"type":"p","text":"Furthermore, the governor claims that George Smith created lollipops in New Haven, Connecticut, in 1908, a claim supported by a ton of news articles and, dare I say, a book. New Haven is a city of outstanding firsts; we know there are claims it was also the site of the invention of the hamburger."},{"type":"p","text":"We say \"claims\" because there are other cities that assert they are the birthplace of the hamburger. Indeed, New Haven is also known as the pizza capital of the world, oops, we mean the US."},{"type":"p","text":"New Haven’s Culinary Fame"},{"type":"p","text":"That is truly great news for New Haven, also referred to as Elm City. And keep in mind that when we talk about New Haven pizza. It is pronounced \"ah-beetz\" if you decide to try it there."},{"type":"p","text":"Grassroots Support for Lollipops"},{"type":"p","text":"Although the highest levels of Congress, including New Haven''s own U.S. Representative Rosa DeLauro, D-3, has endorsed pizza, the general public''s support for lollipops has been a little more grassroots."},{"type":"p","text":"Student Advocacy for State Candy"},{"type":"p","text":"The History Behind the Lollipop"},{"type":"p","text":"Griffin added that Smith registered the trademark for the lollipop name in 1931 and named the candy \"after a racehorse of the time, Lolly Pop.\" Griffin added that Mrs. Robb, his third-grade teacher, attempted to turn PezTM into the official state candy about 14 years ago."},{"type":"p","text":"Sadly, it was killed in committee because, although lollipops aren''t a brand, the state can''t support a product. That''s why I believe lollipops ought to be the official state candy. I hope that''s what you think,\" Griffin wrote. (Pez is the name of the company and the candy; it is based in Orange.)"},{"type":"p","text":"Persistence in Advocacy"},{"type":"p","text":"\"Most states have an official state food, dessert, or even a full meal,\" stated a sixth-grade student who has been fighting for the lollipops for years in his testimony."},{"type":"p","text":"A Unique State Candy"},{"type":"p","text":"But at the time, she asserted that \"no state has a state candy.\"Being one of the few states without any official state food, what better way to catch up with the rest of the world than with lollipops? Imagine tourists traveling to Connecticut to experience a little bit of our history and learn more about lollipops. Being named an official candy can lead to celebrations and festivals honoring the lollipop as a \"delicious aspect of our heritage\" and as a part of Connecticut''s history."},{"type":"p","text":"A Long-Term Goal"},{"type":"p","text":"She stated, \"For the pas"},{"type":"p","text":"t four years, my third-grade class and I have been working on making lollipops, the state candy of Connecticut.\"I think that this year is ours and that we can finally pull through. The student attested, \"Remember to fill your days with laughter, love, and lollipops.\" (keep our dentists in the dark)"},{"type":"p","text":"A Flavorful Future"},{"type":"p","text":"After all this enjoyment, there is one more thing to mention about the new law. It does not specify the flavor of the candy; it just states, \"The lollipop shall be the state candy.\" It seems that the rest of us will have to make that decision. We may also need to follow up with Mrs. Robb''s class."},{"type":"p","text":"Disclaimer: This article is informative and not for promotional purposes. Moreover, the content belongs to the owner and there are no affiliations or marketing motives behind it."},{"type":"p","text":"For media inquiries, please contact:"},{"type":"p","text":"PR Team | pr@eatOS.com | +1 424 401 0184"},{"type":"p","text":"About eatOS"},{"type":"p","text":"Since 2017, eatOS has championed \"Restaurants Made Simple\" through its integrated ecosystem of products. This AI-driven restaurant management technology, tailored for boutique eateries and large-scale chains, boasts an advanced Point of Sale, intuitive kitchen interfaces, table-side ordering and payment solutions, self-service kiosks, and an expansive online ordering and delivery platform. We''re redefining the dining landscape, ensuring efficiency, and elevating guest experiences."},{"type":"p","text":"eatOS POS Inc. | 1111 Brickell Avenue FL 10, Miami, FL 33131 | eatOS.com"}]', 'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/0d9b20_8d4503de12cb4168aaa0696a72d55258~mv2.jpg/v1/fill/w_1920,h_1080,al_c,q_90/Blog%202.jpg', 'Industry News', 'eatOS Staff', '2024-06-11', 'published'),
  ('top-restaurant-globally-for-2024-announced-in-las-vegas', 'Top Restaurant Globally for 2024 Announced in Las Vegas', 'World''s 50 Best Restaurants Names Disfrutar Global Champion for 2024', '[{"type":"h2","text":"World''s 50 Best Restaurants Names Disfrutar Global Champion for 2024"},{"type":"p","text":"Chef Tomos Parry of London''s Brat and Mountain restaurants joined chef James Trees on Monday at Esther''s Kitchen, his downtown restaurant, for one of the 50 Best Signature Sessions. The lunch that the chefs served lasted for four hours."},{"type":"p","text":"Virgilio Martinez, co-chef and owner of Central in Lima, and Sarah Thompson, executive chef of Casa Playa on the property, participated in a Tuesday morning conversation at Wynn. In 2023, Central ranked as the best restaurant globally."},{"type":"p","text":"Thompson talked about the week''s opportunities and excitement. ‘It is vitally crucial to seize the moment. These partnerships with the world''s top chefs advance the cause. These chefs are inspiring the city and the restaurants with their passions.’"},{"type":"p","text":"Martinez discussed his restaurant philosophy among other things.‘ We try to cook ideas at Central, not recipes. Our goal is to prepare culture. Being the best restaurant in Central that we can be has always been our primary objective.’"},{"type":"p","text":"From Plants to Animals"},{"type":"p","text":"50 Best Talk, Treasure Hunt: The Quest for Culinary Gold, was held at Wynn. According to the talk, there are many ways to create gastronomic gold, such as repurposing simple plant-based ingredients, revitalizing age-old cooking methods, fostering the growth of underappreciated chefs, reevaluating the conventional restaurant hierarchy, and using the entire fish, from the snout to the tail, in culinary creations."},{"type":"p","text":"Chef Daniel Humm of Eleven Madison Park in New York City, the first plant-based restaurant to receive three Michelin stars, was one of the eight chefs and restaurateurs who took the stage. He discussed some of the difficulties Eleven Madison Park encountered upon reopening in June 2021 with a menu focused primarily on plants, having previously gained notoriety for its foie gras, duck, and lobster dishes."},{"type":"p","text":"\"We were like, ''Oh my God, where do we start?'' as soon as we entered the kitchen. What are our new milk and butter? What materials make up the stocks? We started by making our pantry before we started on our menu."},{"type":"p","text":"\"It became political when the plant-based menu was announced. Meat suppliers wrote to us, saying, \"This will never work; they will never deliver to me when I need their meat again.\" We received some extremely critical articles and reviews. But Eleven Madison Park will cease to exist if we don''t adapt."},{"type":"p","text":"Using the Whole Fish"},{"type":"p","text":"Josh Niland, a.k.a. The \"fish butcher\" and chef-owner of Saint Peter in Sydney, discussed how half of a fish usually ends up in the trash in restaurants during the Culinary Gold session. \"We''re using secondary cuts of fish, building out all the things you can do with fish,\" says Saint Peter. We see fish too often as just two filets. What can we do with the remaining fish?"},{"type":"p","text":"A possible solution is to grill the collar and head. Another is to use the eyes to create \"chips.\" Niland described the bite as crispy and salty. The first question posed to the crowd after the meal was what they thought of the chips at first? We declared, \"Fisher eye.\" That encouraged the subsequent group of patrons to enter the eatery."},{"type":"p","text":"Fish bladder ricotta cheese was an unsuccessful experiment. It was rather disgusting, Niland remarked. People at the talk were served what the chef described as an ice cream sandwich. It tasted and felt like a version without dairy or gluten. Not horrible, but not very noteworthy."},{"type":"p","text":"However, the ice cream sandwich turned into a miracle when Niland revealed that the cake was made of fish bones and the filling was made of fish eye vitreous humor."},{"type":"p","text":"A World Feast"},{"type":"p","text":"Three days of events are scheduled for the World''s 50 Best week following the ceremony. These include pop-ups and collaborations at Resorts World''s Indulge Festival and Wynn''s Revelry Festival''s Icons Dinner, which features some of the world''s most renowned chefs."},{"type":"p","text":"On Saturday, the week comes to an end with Revelry''s centerpiece event, The Feast, which brings together four distinct culinary genres: wood-fire rotisserie and barbecue, Mediterranean cooking, coastal Mexican dishes, and Tokyo street food."},{"type":"p","text":"Disclaimer: This article is informative and not for promotional purposes. Moreover, the content belongs to the owner and there are no affiliations or marketing motives behind it."},{"type":"p","text":"For media inquiries, please contact:"},{"type":"p","text":"PR Team | pr@eatOS.com | +1 424 401 0184"},{"type":"p","text":"About eatOS"},{"type":"p","text":"Since 2017, eatOS has championed \"Restaurants Made Simple\" through its integrated ecosystem of products. This AI-driven restaurant management technology, tailored for boutique eateries and large-scale chains, boasts an advanced Point of Sale, intuitive kitchen interfaces, table-side ordering and payment solutions, self-service kiosks, and an expansive online ordering and delivery platform. We''re redefining the dining landscape, ensuring efficiency, and elevating guest experiences."},{"type":"p","text":"eatOS POS Inc. | 1111 Brickell Avenue FL 10, Miami, FL 33131 | eatOS.com"}]', 'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/0d9b20_7f77e02646d340d89c3c356957297c9e~mv2.jpg/v1/fill/w_3000,h_2000,al_c,q_90/Blog%201.jpg', 'Industry News', 'eatOS Staff', '2024-06-10', 'published'),
  ('eatos-introduces-groundbreaking-quick-service-solutions-to-boost-efficiency', 'eatOS Introduces Groundbreaking Quick Service Solutions to Boost Efficiency', 'Revolutionizing Quick Service: eatOS''s Innovative Solutions Drive Efficiency and Elevate Customer Satisfaction', '[{"type":"p","text":"FOR IMMEDIATE RELEASE"},{"type":"p","text":"Los Angeles, CA - June 5, 2024- In a dynamic and fast-paced industry, eatOS emerges as a game-changer with its innovative Quick Service Solutions, providing restaurants with a versatile Point of Sale (POS) system ideal for Quick-Service and Fast-Casual concepts."},{"type":"p","text":"In the contemporary culinary landscape, the ascent of Quick Service Restaurants (QSRs) has been nothing short of remarkable. As consumer preferences increasingly lean towards fast, convenient, and high-quality dining experiences, the demand for Quick Service Restaurants has surged. In response to this dynamic shift, eatOS emerges as a technological pioneer, spearheading innovation to meet the unique challenges of the restaurant business, particularly in the Quick Service sector."},{"type":"p","text":"At the forefront of this technological revolution is eatOS''s specially designed Point of Sale (POS) system, meticulously crafted to cater specifically to the demanding nature of Quick Service Restaurants. With speed and efficiency as top priorities, eatOS technology ensures seamless and rapid order processing, enabling QSRs to meet the swift expectations of their customers. Here are its unique features:"},{"type":"p","text":"Versatile POS System"},{"type":"ul","items":["eatOS offers a versatile POS system tailored for Quick-Service and Fast-Casual restaurants.","Designed to cater to unique business needs, ensuring agility and adaptability in any scenario."]},{"type":"p","text":"Payment-Ready Anytime, Anywhere"},{"type":"ul","items":["eatOS ensures payment readiness for customers ordering at the counter or on-the-go.","The powerful, cloud-based ecosystem efficiently manages Quick-Service Restaurants, even during connectivity challenges.","Eliminates the impact of wifi outages, enabling uninterrupted service."]},{"type":"p","text":"Seamless Restaurant Management"},{"type":"ul","items":["eatOS simplifies restaurant management and payment processing.","Operates seamlessly in online and offline modes, guaranteeing no loss of sales in the absence of a stable internet connection.","The multi-user and -device environment promote effortless collaboration among staff."]},{"type":"p","text":"The \"Keep Them Coming Back\" aspect of eatOS is defined by its menu management feature, which plays a pivotal role in elevating the speed and efficiency of guest service. This feature seamlessly streamlines communication within the restaurant, ensuring precise and prompt delivery of orders. By enhancing the overall dining experience through improved operational efficiency, eatOS encourages customer satisfaction and loyalty, creating an environment that entices patrons to return."},{"type":"p","text":"Crucially, eatOS technology doesn''t just address the current needs of QSRs; it anticipates and adapts to the future landscape of the industry. As consumer trends evolve and technology continues to shape dining experiences, eatOS remains committed to providing cutting-edge solutions that keep Quick Service Restaurants ahead of the curve."},{"type":"p","text":"\"With eatOS, we aim to empower Quick-Service and Fast-Casual restaurants with the tools they need to thrive in a competitive industry. Our solutions are not just versatile and efficient; they are designed to keep your business running smoothly in any circumstance,\" said Akash Aurora, CEO."},{"type":"p","text":"For media inquiries, please contact:"},{"type":"p","text":"PR Team | pr@eatOS.com | +1 424 401 0184"},{"type":"p","text":"About eatOS"},{"type":"p","text":"Since 2017, eatOS has championed \"Restaurants Made Simple\" through its integrated ecosystem of products. This AI-driven restaurant management technology, tailored for boutique eateries and large-scale chains, boasts an advanced Point of Sale, intuitive kitchen interfaces, table-side ordering and payment solutions, self-service kiosks, and an expansive online ordering and delivery platform. We''re redefining the dining landscape, ensuring efficiency, and elevating guest experiences."},{"type":"p","text":"eatOS POS Inc. | 1111 Brickell Avenue FL 10, Miami, FL 33131 | eatOS.com"}]', 'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/7b1e9b_011aa208427f48f48d403395fc6f0f46~mv2.jpg/v1/fill/w_1080,h_1080,al_c,q_85/Quick%20Service.jpg', 'Product News', 'eatOS Staff', '2024-06-05', 'published'),
  ('eatos-reveals-state-of-the-art-hardware-solutions-crafted-to-revolutionize-your-business-processes', 'eatOS Reveals State-of-the-Art Hardware Solutions Crafted to Revolutionize Your Business Processes', 'Growing with Your Business - Easily Expand Your Hardware Infrastructure for Long-Term Success', '[{"type":"p","text":"FOR IMMEDIATE RELEASE"},{"type":"p","text":"Los Angeles, CA - June 3, 2024- Today, eatOS, a trailblazer in hospitality technology, proudly unveils its comprehensive suite of hardware solutions designed to transform the way restaurants operate. From state-of-the-art Point of Sale (POS) systems to intuitive Self Ordering Kiosks and advanced Kitchen Display Screens, eatOS is committed to providing powerful and seamlessly integrated hardware that caters to the diverse needs of Quick and Full-Service Restaurants."},{"type":"p","text":"The hardware used in a restaurant is the backbone of its operations, influencing everything from order processing and payment transactions to kitchen workflows and customer engagement. Choosing the right hardware is not just a matter of functionality; it''s about future-proofing your business to adapt to the ever-changing demands of the industry."},{"type":"p","text":"At eatOS, we recognize the pivotal role that hardware plays in the success of a restaurant. Our commitment to innovation drives us to deliver cutting-edge hardware solutions that address the specific needs of the modern and more innovative food industry."},{"type":"p","text":"Point of Sale (POS) Hardware: eatOS offers a strong solution for Quick and Full-Service Restaurants with its cloud-based management and payment system. The POS hardware, including brands like Elo®, Clover®, and HP®, suits all restaurant types perfectly."},{"type":"p","text":"Self Ordering Kiosk: Elo®''s Self Ordering Kiosk effortlessly integrates with eatOS, ensuring a smooth ordering experience for customers and staff."},{"type":"p","text":"Receipt & Kitchen Printers: Star Micronics® provides a tailored range of printing solutions, linking your Point of Sale and Kitchen to top-notch restaurant printers for streamlined order processing."},{"type":"p","text":"Kitchen Display Screens: Elo®''s Kitchen and Expo Screens, with open frame touchscreens, are the last step for restaurant teams, bringing together all elements of each customer''s order for smooth order fulfillment."},{"type":"p","text":"Payment Acceptance: eatOS provides compact yet powerful EMV, Contactless debit, and credit card readers, ensuring secure and efficient payment processing with maximum data protection for restaurants."},{"type":"p","text":"Kitchen Display Software: eatOS introduces Kitchen Display Software, purpose-built for kitchens with touch screen hardware, ensuring efficient operations and backed by a 3-year warranty."},{"type":"p","text":"Self Service Kiosk: eatOS''s Self Service Kiosk seamlessly integrates with the Point of Sale and Kitchen Display Screen, reducing costs and offering a convenient self-service option for modern customers at the store or table."},{"type":"p","text":"Accessories: Enhance your restaurant business with advanced hardware from world-leading brands such as Elo®, Apple®, Star Micronics®, HP®, Clover®, Square®, Samsung®, Lenovo®, and more. Discover which eatOS product works best for your restaurant."},{"type":"p","text":"\"eatOS is more than a technology provider; we are a partner in the success of your restaurant. Our hardware solutions are meticulously designed to meet the demands of the modern food industry, providing the tools you need to stay ahead and thrive,\" said Akash Aurora, CEO."},{"type":"p","text":"For media inquiries, please contact:"},{"type":"p","text":"PR Team | pr@eatOS.com | +1 424 401 0184"},{"type":"p","text":"About eatOS"},{"type":"p","text":"Since 2017, eatOS has championed \"Restaurants Made Simple\" through its integrated ecosystem of products. This AI-driven restaurant management technology, tailored for boutique eateries and large-scale chains, boasts an advanced Point of Sale, intuitive kitchen interfaces, table-side ordering and payment solutions, self-service kiosks, and an expansive online ordering and delivery platform. We''re redefining the dining landscape, ensuring efficiency, and elevating guest experiences."},{"type":"p","text":"eatOS POS Inc. | 1111 Brickell Avenue FL 10, Miami, FL 33131 | eatOS.com"}]', 'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/7b1e9b_e1bb318286c24d159239d46caaf3f1c2~mv2.jpg/v1/fill/w_1080,h_1080,al_c,q_85/State-of-the-Art%20Hardware%20Square.jpg', 'Product News', 'eatOS Staff', '2024-05-03', 'published'),
  ('eatos-presents-fully-autonomous-and-automated-delivery-system-revolutionizing-restaurant-service', 'eatOS Presents Fully Autonomous and Automated Delivery System Revolutionizing Restaurant Service', 'Introducing ServeBot - Your Ultimate Restaurant Assistant', '[{"type":"p","text":"FOR IMMEDIATE RELEASE"},{"type":"p","text":"Miami, FL - February 29, 2024 - In a groundbreaking move towards enhancing restaurant efficiency, eatOS introduces ServeBot, a state-of-the-art fully autonomous, and automated delivery system. ServeBot is set to revolutionize the restaurant industry by seamlessly managing dish and liquid delivery, freeing up staff for more meaningful customer interactions."},{"type":"p","text":"As the demand for autonomous and automated delivery solutions rises, eatOS emerges as the answer to the industry''s evolving needs. Integrating seamlessly with ServeBot, eatOS complements this cutting-edge technology by providing a comprehensive restaurant operating system. eatOS streamline order management, inventory control, and customer engagement, ensuring that restaurants are equipped to meet the demands of the modern dining landscape. Its best features are the following:"},{"type":"p","text":"Fully Autonomous System: ServeBot leads in innovation, providing a fully autonomous system that handles a diverse menu of over 15 dishes and liquids. Its large tray capacity and custom tray integration offer a versatile solution for various restaurant types."},{"type":"p","text":"Collective Automation for Seamless Workflow: ServeBot''s collective automation streamlines communication between restaurant units, like the kitchen, bar, and serving stations, ensuring smooth processes, optimized workflow, and reduced errors or delays."},{"type":"p","text":"Weight-Responsive Auto Return: ServeBot''s auto-return feature swiftly brings it back to the designated location after a task, eliminating manual intervention and allowing staff to focus on critical responsibilities, saving time and effort."},{"type":"p","text":"Swift, Agile, and Space-Saving Design: ServeBot''s sleek, compact design effortlessly navigates tight spaces, ensuring quick service in crowded restaurants. It''s swift movement and space-saving design seamlessly integrate into layouts without disruptions."},{"type":"p","text":"Enhanced Operational Efficiency and Reduced Labor Hours: Restaurant operations transform with the introduction of ServeBot, automating tasks such as order delivery and table clearing to cut labor hours and enhance efficiency, leading to substantial cost savings for establishments."},{"type":"p","text":"Improved Retention and Prioritized Employee Wellness: Continuous physical strain is eliminated by ServeBot, promoting enhanced retention and satisfaction. Specialized tasks can be focused on by team members, fostering a healthier work environment and prioritizing well-being."},{"type":"p","text":"ServeBot is poised to redefine restaurant service by combining cutting-edge technology with practical solutions, providing an unparalleled dining experience for both customers and staff. Embrace the future of restaurant management with ServeBot''s autonomous and automated delivery system."},{"type":"p","text":"\"As we unveil ServeBot''s revolutionary capabilities, we are not just introducing a product but ushering in a transformative era for the restaurant industry. This synergy of ServeBot and eatOS reflects our commitment to efficiency, innovation, and unparalleled customer experiences. We envision a future where restaurants thrive in a tech-driven landscape, meeting the demands of today''s dynamic dining scene.\" said Akash Aurora, CEO."},{"type":"p","text":"For media inquiries, please contact:"},{"type":"p","text":"PR Team | pr@eatOS.com | +1 424 401 0184"},{"type":"p","text":"About eatOS"},{"type":"p","text":"Since 2017, eatOS has championed \"Restaurants Made Simple\" through its integrated ecosystem of products. This AI-driven restaurant management technology, tailored for boutique eateries and large-scale chains, boasts an advanced Point of Sale, intuitive kitchen interfaces, table-side ordering and payment solutions, self-service kiosks, and an expansive online ordering and delivery platform. We''re redefining the dining landscape, ensuring efficiency, and elevating guest experiences."},{"type":"p","text":"eatOS POS Inc. | 1111 Brickell Avenue FL 10, Miami, FL 33131 | eatOS.com"}]', 'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/73c1f0_654763910159432b87a4a82ce0b13602~mv2.jpg/v1/fill/w_1080,h_1080,al_c,q_85/blog-12.jpg', 'Product News', 'eatOS Staff', '2024-02-29', 'published'),
  ('eatos-transforms-restaurant-operations-with-voiceos', 'eatOS Transforms Restaurant Operations with VoiceOS', 'A Feature That Optimizes Processes and Elevates Customer Interactions', '[{"type":"p","text":"FOR IMMEDIATE RELEASE"},{"type":"p","text":"Miami, FL | February 14, 2024 - eatOS, a top-tier vendor of restaurant technology solutions, today announced the launch of VoiceOS, a groundbreaking new feature that empowers restaurants to take orders, process payments, and manage customer interactions using voice commands. VoiceOS is designed to optimize processes, elevate customer interactions, and maximize revenue generation for restaurants of all sizes."},{"type":"p","text":"How VoiceOS Reinvents Restaurant Operations"},{"type":"p","text":"VoiceOS is an AI-powered voice assistant that seamlessly integrates with the eatOS POS system. With VoiceOS, restaurant staff can simply speak their orders into the microphone to quickly and accurately enter orders, process payments, and manage customer requests. This hands-free approach allows staff to focus on providing exceptional customer service while maintaining efficiency during busy periods."},{"type":"p","text":"Advantages of VoiceOS for Restaurants"},{"type":"p","text":"VoiceOS offers a multitude of advantages for restaurants, including:"},{"type":"ul","items":["Increased Order Precision: VoiceOS reduces the risk of errors by eliminating the need for manual data entry.","Improved Efficiency: VoiceOS optimizes order taking and payment processing, allowing staff to serve more customers in less time.","Elevated Customer Experience: VoiceOS enables staff to provide faster and more attentive service.","Reduced Labor Costs: VoiceOS can help restaurants reduce labor costs by eliminating the need for dedicated order takers.","Improved Productivity: VoiceOS allows staff to multitask more effectively, boosting overall productivity."]},{"type":"p","text":"A Paradigm Shift for the Restaurant Industry"},{"type":"p","text":"VoiceOS is a paradigm shift for the restaurant industry, revolutionizing the way restaurants operate and interact with their customers. By leveraging the power of AI, eatOS is empowering restaurants to achieve new levels of efficiency, customer satisfaction, and revenue generation."},{"type":"p","text":"Availability"},{"type":"p","text":"VoiceOS is available now as an add-on feature for eatOS POS customers. To learn more about VoiceOS and how it can benefit your restaurant, please visit www.eatOS.com"},{"type":"p","text":"For media inquiries, please contact:"},{"type":"p","text":"PR Team | pr@eatOS.com | +1 424 401 0184"},{"type":"p","text":"About eatOS"},{"type":"p","text":"Since 2017, eatOS has championed \"Restaurants Made Simple\" through its integrated ecosystem of products. This AI-driven restaurant management technology, tailored for boutique eateries and large-scale chains, boasts an advanced Point of Sale, intuitive kitchen interfaces, table-side ordering and payment solutions, self-service kiosks, and an expansive online ordering and delivery platform. We''re redefining the dining landscape, ensuring efficiency, and elevating guest experiences."},{"type":"p","text":"eatOS POS Inc. | 1111 Brickell Avenue FL 10, Miami, FL 33131 | eatOS.com"}]', 'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/73c1f0_e58d2a082f1e4412aae7557b15371648~mv2.jpg/v1/fill/w_1080,h_1080,al_c,q_85/blog-10.jpg', 'Product News', 'eatOS Staff', '2024-02-14', 'published'),
  ('eatos-to-showcase-innovative-restaurant-technology-solutions-at-nrf-2024-in-partnership-with-sunmi', 'eatOS to Showcase Innovative Restaurant Technology Solutions at NRF 2024 in Partnership with SUNMI', 'Unveiling Tomorrow''s Dining Experience: eatOS and SUNMI''s Showcase at NRF 2024', '[{"type":"h2","text":"Unveiling Tomorrow''s Dining Experience: eatOS and SUNMI''s Showcase at NRF 2024"},{"type":"p","text":"FOR IMMEDIATE RELEASE"},{"type":"p","text":"Miami, FL | February 8, 2024 - eatOS, a leading provider of restaurant technology solutions, is excited to announce its participation in the upcoming NRF Retail 2024 event, taking place from January 14-16, 2024, at the Jacob Javits Center in New York City. In partnership with SUNMI, a global leader in smart hardware solutions, eatOS will showcase its latest innovations in restaurant technology at booth #3165 on the show floor."},{"type":"p","text":"NRF Retail 2024 is the world''s largest retail event, bringing together thousands of industry leaders to explore the latest trends and technologies shaping the future of retail. eatOS and SUNMI are thrilled to be a part of this event and to share their vision for how technology can transform the restaurant industry."},{"type":"p","text":"At the show, eatOS and SUNMI will be demonstrating a range of innovative solutions designed to help restaurants streamline operations, improve customer experience, and increase profitability. These solutions include:"},{"type":"ul","items":["eatOS point-of-sale (POS) system: A user-friendly and powerful POS system that enables restaurants to manage orders, payments, and inventory with ease.","SUNMI smart hardwar e: A suite of smart hardware devices, including tablets, printers, and kiosks, that seamlessly integrate with the eatOS POS system.","eatOS data analytics: A comprehensive data analytics platform that provides restaurants with insights into their business performance so they can make data-driven decisions."]},{"type":"p","text":"In addition to these innovative solutions, eatOS and SUNMI will also be offering demos of their latest features and integrations, as well as hosting a series of educational sessions on how to use technology to improve restaurant operations."},{"type":"p","text":"eatOS and SUNMI invite all to visit their booth at NRF Retail 2024 to experience the future of restaurant technology firsthand."},{"type":"p","text":"For media inquiries, please contact:"},{"type":"p","text":"PR Team | pr@eatOS.com | +1 424 401 0184"},{"type":"p","text":"About eatOS"},{"type":"p","text":"Since 2017, eatOS has championed \"Restaurants Made Simple\" through its integrated ecosystem of products. This AI-driven restaurant management technology, tailored for boutique eateries and large-scale chains, boasts an advanced Point of Sale, intuitive kitchen interfaces, table-side ordering and payment solutions, self-service kiosks, and an expansive online ordering and delivery platform. We''re redefining the dining landscape, ensuring efficiency, and elevating guest experiences."},{"type":"p","text":"eatOS POS Inc. | 1111 Brickell Avenue FL 10, Miami, FL 33131 | eatOS.com"}]', 'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/73c1f0_746c2a5224c54ee4a3e385e995660e1a~mv2.jpg/v1/fill/w_1080,h_1080,al_c,q_85/blog-8.jpg', 'Event News', 'eatOS Staff', '2024-02-08', 'published'),
  ('eatos-launches-cloud-enabled-enterprise-point-of-sale-technology-cloud', 'eatOS Launches Cloud-Enabled Enterprise Point-of-Sale Technology Cloud', 'Enterprise ecosystems operates on the cloud with online, offline and on-prem capability.', '[{"type":"h2","text":"Enterprise ecosystems operates on the cloud with online, offline and on-prem capability."},{"type":"p","text":"FOR IMMEDIATE RELEASE"},{"type":"p","text":"Miami, FL - August 10, 2023- eatOS unveils its Enterprise Point of Sale (POS) Technology cloud, tailor-made for the dynamic needs of expansive enterprise restaurant with 50 or more locations."},{"type":"p","text":"This state-of-the-art cloud enterprise Point of Sale (POS) heralds a new era in operational agility and guest satisfaction, innovating Hospitality with Advanced Cloud Solutions."},{"type":"p","text":"eatOS'' Enterprise Point of Sale (POS) Technology cloud represents the pinnacle of innovation in enterprise management. It boasts a suite of features designed to streamline order processing, oversee inventory with precision, manage staff schedules efficiently, and elevate guest service experiences. The result is a marked decrease in waiting times, a boost in service standards, and more fluid operational processes."},{"type":"p","text":"Understanding the diverse requirements of large-scale enterprises, eatOS has developed a Enterprise Point of Sale (POS) Technology cloud that scales with ease. Ideal for multi-location enterprises, the enterprise cloud offers consistent, evolving support as businesses expand."},{"type":"p","text":"Pioneering Features of the eatOS Enterprise Point of Sale (POS) Technology cloud Include:"},{"type":"p","text":"Enhanced Customer Engagement - The enterprise cloud introduces advanced capabilities like online ordering using a white-labbeled app and integration with various delivery platforms, and the creation of personalized guest profiles, ensuring every customer interaction is exceptional and tailored."},{"type":"p","text":"Unified Management Ecosystem - This comprehensive suite brings together critical aspects of enterprise management including guest relations, staff coordination, marketing, financial oversight, and menu management into a single, streamlined platform, significantly boosting operational effectiveness."},{"type":"p","text":"Streamlined Staff Operations - The enterprise cloud simplifies essential staff tasks such as time tracking, schedule management, and payroll, enabling staff to devote more energy to quality service and product delivery."},{"type":"p","text":"The Enterprise Point of Sale (POS) Technology cloud by eatOS is a game-changer, offering an all-encompassing, adaptable solution with pioneering features for bespoke customer service, and strong online and offline functionalities, ensuring seamless service continuity."},{"type":"p","text":"Empowering Teams and Enhancing Operations - The enterprise cloud is designed for quick, intuitive staff training. It minimizes operational errors, integrates efficiently with online and third-party ordering systems, and includes features like server scorecards to motivate staff, ultimately enriching the dining experience."},{"type":"p","text":"Customizable to Your Unique Requirements - The enterprise cloud is versatile, functioning across various operating systems and devices, and offers seamless integration with chosen payment providers. It supports distinct ordering workflows and is designed to create a comprehensive, customized guest experience."},{"type":"p","text":"Data-Driven Decision Making - The enterprise cloud provides immediate access to sales data, helping to optimize labor costs and enhance profit margins. Its robust reporting features include on-demand access and simple exporting options for seamless accounting software integration."},{"type":"p","text":"Subscription and Features - eatOS''s enterprise cloud subscription plans include essential features to ensure restaurant success, along with consistent software updates, online training resources, and a comprehensive self-service help portal."},{"type":"p","text":"Why Opt for Enterprise Point of Sale (POS) Technology cloud by eatOS?"},{"type":"p","text":"Versatility - Compatible with multiple devices and systems, ensuring seamless integration."},{"type":"p","text":"Reliability - Constructed on the Amazon, Google and Azure cloud platform, offering secure and dependable service."},{"type":"p","text":"Invitation to Experience Enterprise Point of Sale (POS) Technology cloud by eatOS - eatOS invites businesses to request a demo to explore the transformative capabilities and various editions of the Cloud POS."},{"type":"p","text":"Akash Aurora, CEO of eatOS, shares his vision \"The introduction of our Enterprise Point of Sale (POS) Technology cloud signifies a transformative leap in restaurant management. We are committed to equipping businesses with advanced tools to enhance operations and enrich customer interactions.\""},{"type":"p","text":"For media inquiries, please contact:"},{"type":"p","text":"PR Team | pr@eatOS.com | +1 424 401 0184"},{"type":"p","text":"About eatOS"},{"type":"p","text":"Since 2017, eatOS has championed \"Restaurants Made Simple\" through its integrated ecosystem of products. This AI-driven restaurant management technology, tailored for boutique eateries and large-scale chains, boasts an advanced Point of Sale, intuitive kitchen interfaces, table-side ordering and payment solutions, self-service kiosks, and an expansive online ordering and delivery platform. We''re redefining the dining landscape, ensuring efficiency, and elevating guest experiences."},{"type":"p","text":"eatOS POS Inc. | 1111 Brickell Avenue FL 10, Miami, FL 33131 | eatOS.com"}]', 'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/7b1e9b_4ff301a180d142d496f8d33d958e760d~mv2.jpg/v1/fill/w_1080,h_1080,al_c,q_85/Enterprise%20Square.jpg', 'Product News', 'eatOS Staff', '2023-08-10', 'published');
